This was my first acsension, but didnt look like it for a long time. I
worked on the character a bit, but by the time of the quest, the amour class
was still pathetic but i did have the +5 Mjollnir by then (found in a bones
level). Without this bones level, it is highly unlikely that I ever would 
have acsended. I found the Snickersnee in a shop, and got my pet to steal
it, and obtained Dragonbane from sacrificing to my god (this was before I
had Mjlollnir).
Actually, that could have been the other way around !

There was only one lucky escape where I needed an amulet of life saving. I 
coked on my food on about level 26 on the way back up after getting the amulet
(phew!).

I never had abag of holding, and had to ditch a lot of gold at the bottom 
of the dungeon - hence the lack of it at the end ! I constantly seemed to
be burdened or stressed as a result, even with the 25 strength. My wishes
at the castle were wasted as I never really got what I wanted, and I didnt
have any left at the end (I went for 3 of genocide and 3 of enchant armour
but got one in either case).

When I had got the amulet I had a ring of conflict which helped immensely.
The wiz's summoned creatures fought themselves, making killing the wiz a lot
easier. I had posted a message asking which weapon to use. Someone said that
the Tsurugi was best, and I quite agree. Although I bit later on I reverted 
to the Mjollnir so that I could use the shield of reflection on the 
Elemental planes. I has one hell of a problem finding the stairs to Vlad's
tower - hence the high number of turns required. It is so easy to miss
the stairs, or have a rock on top of them or make them not visible. 

Orcus and Yeenoghu were a bit tricky as Orcus summoned the other up, I was
blinded and I didnt have my unicorn horn handy. Anyway, orcus zapped his 
wand which bounced off my shield and hit Yeenoghu and helped me a bit ! 

The elemental planes were tricky since they were new to me. I found the portals
reasonably easily except on the Water level, until i realised that a wand
of secret door detection could help me. I hadnt identified this wand at this
stage, so just zapped the unknown ones. Fortunately it worked with the
first one, so I got off that level (i was on it for quite a while before i
worked that out).

The Astral plane was suprisingly easy, although I forgot to change amulets from
the magical breathing to the life saving. I only met pestilence and the first 
altar I found was the lawful one.

The game balance was pretty good. I didnt have much of the problem with
the teleport in hell, but the ring of conflict helped ever so much.

I'm now going to see what I can do with the other 11 classes !

